CORE
main.cpp
--winx64 --cpp17 --pointer-check --malloc-may-fail --malloc-fail-null
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ an owned copy: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ a fresh copy: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ the same string: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ destroyed: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ shared: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.6\] line \d+ a code page: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.7\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Models of __std_exception_copy, __std_exception_destroy and
__std_fs_code_page, which the MSVC runtime library defines.  Natively, the
test runs with stand-ins for them.
